&lt;p&gt;Takealot.com, a leading South African online retailer, is looking for a highly talented&lt;strong&gt; Seller Sales Manager, Cross-Border Selling&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;to join our team in Cape Town.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us.&amp;nbsp; We offer a market related, Total Remuneration Package which allows full flexibility according to your needs, a great work environment and a promise that you won’t be bored as long as you are prepared for a challenge and want to build something great.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a senior position reporting to the &lt;strong&gt;Head of Cross-Border Commerce.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Role Purpose&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Seller Sales Manager leads and manages the Sales &amp;amp; Account Manager team responsible for acquiring new international sellers and growing the Takealot cross-border seller base. This role exists to provide strategic direction, structured pipeline oversight, and active coaching to ensure the team consistently meets seller acquisition and revenue targets. The Manager operates at the intersection of team leadership, sales operations, and commercial strategy — owning the end-to-end seller acquisition funnel while also contributing to the broader cross-border commercial strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Leadership &amp;amp; People Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Directly manage the Sales &amp;amp; Account Manager team and business development team; set individual targets, conduct regular 1:1s, provide structured coaching, and lead performance reviews; create a high-performance, seller-obsessed team culture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Seller Acquisition Strategy:&lt;/strong&gt; Define and own the go-to-market strategy for international seller recruitment, including target seller profiles (by category, country of origin, scale), outreach channels, and value proposition messaging.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pipeline Management &amp;amp; Forecasting:&lt;/strong&gt; Oversee the team&#39;s CRM pipeline; ensure pipeline health (coverage ratios, stage accuracy, deal velocity); produce weekly and monthly sales forecasts for senior leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Target Setting &amp;amp; Quota Allocation:&lt;/strong&gt; Translate team-level seller acquisition and GMV targets into individual quotas for each Sales &amp;amp; Account Manager; track attainment and intervene early where individuals are at risk of missing targets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Sales Process &amp;amp; Playbook Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and continuously refine the end-to-end seller sales process — from lead generation and qualification through to onboarding and first-sale activation; document processes in a scalable sales playbook.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Collaboration:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with the Aggregator Partnerships Manager to ensure seamless handoff of partner-referred sellers; collaborate with the Analyst on funnel reporting; work with Takealot&#39;s seller onboarding, legal, and compliance teams to remove friction in the seller sign-up process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Recruitment &amp;amp; Team Scaling:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with HR to recruit, onboard, and develop additional Sales &amp;amp; Account Managers as the team scales; define role profiles and competency frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Market Intelligence &amp;amp; Feedback Loop:&lt;/strong&gt; Gather structured feedback from prospective sellers on barriers to joining Takealot (fees, compliance complexity, logistics, etc.); synthesise insights and advocate for product/policy changes that improve seller conversion.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Executive Reporting:&lt;/strong&gt; Prepare and present monthly and quarterly commercial performance updates for the Head of Cross-Border Selling and senior Takealot leadership, covering acquisition trends, pipeline, revenue ramp, and market insights.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications &amp;amp; Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Commerce, Business Administration, Marketing, or a related field; MBA advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum 6–8 years of sales experience, with at least 3 years in a team leadership or sales management role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven track record of consistently meeting or exceeding sales quotas in a B2B or marketplace sales environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in e-commerce, marketplace platforms, or technology sales is strongly preferred.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to build and scale sales teams in a high-growth or greenfield environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with CRM systems (e.g. Salesforce, HubSpot, or equivalent); experience designing sales processes and pipeline governance frameworks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with cross-border e-commerce dynamics, international seller communities, or marketplace ecosystems is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desired Skills &amp;amp; Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Inspirational people leader — energises and develops team members, creates accountability without micromanagement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen with the ability to think strategically and execute tactically.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data-driven decision-maker who uses pipeline metrics and funnel analytics to coach and intervene.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent communicator — able to influence senior stakeholders internally and build credibility with prospective international sellers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Resilient and adaptable; comfortable with the ambiguity of building a new team and function from scratch.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of personal drive and ownership — treats team targets as personal commitments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding of South African marketplace dynamics and competitive landscape (Checkers Sixty60, Makro, Shein direct, etc.) is advantageous.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Speak Mandarin is highly advantageous&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Environment:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Takealot.com employees are entrepreneurial and dynamic, smart, customer-centric, fun and have the shared ambition of takealot.com being the leading e-commerce company in Africa.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We have fun, work hard, take ownership, work in teams to create solutions, and are always open to direct feedback/new ideas on where we can improve&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are short on ego and high on output&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We are doers and not only thinkers, it’s all in the execution after all&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We love what we do and what we are creating&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We seek to Employ an &lt;strong&gt;Extra Ordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt; who:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is respectful but forthright&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is an expert at doing, who can not only design but also execute&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is analytical, able to use data to make decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is competitive, self-directed and strive to be the BEST (GREAT requires a lot of work and does not only happen during business hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;passionate about the potential of e-commerce&lt;/strong&gt; and delivering a&lt;strong&gt; world-class customer experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;entrepreneurial, thrives under change&lt;/strong&gt; and accepts it is a constant and always&lt;strong&gt; looks for solutions&lt;/strong&gt; to do something better and faster&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is business SMART. Able to think about problems from a business perspective using technical and product input;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is curious and challenge the status quo&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is innovative and enjoys iteration&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is collaborative&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;will be at the cutting edge of developing new concepts for takealot.com&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;thinks like an owner&lt;/strong&gt; of the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;is &lt;strong&gt;SMART, has INTEGRITY&lt;/strong&gt; and is &lt;strong&gt;HARD WORKING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you meet the above criteria and are an&lt;strong&gt; Extraordinary Mind&lt;/strong&gt;, come and join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Takealot is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Applicants from the previously disadvantaged groups and people with disabilities will be given preference.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Takealot.com, South Africa&#39;s leading online retailer, is looking for a highly talented Senior Database Administrator (DBA) to join the Engineering &amp;amp; Product team based in Cape Town, South Africa.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are a young, dynamic, hyper-growth company looking for smart, creative, hard-working people with integrity to join us!&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Think you&#39;ve been challenged before? Think again!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Scale: 4 million happy shoppers shop online on takealot.com. Show them what you can do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn: We work with the best of the best, and then some. Code alongside industry leaders and upskill in record time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Grow: Expand your career in the fast-growing Takealot Group: takealot.com, Mr D, and TFS. We like to promote from within: Here&#39;s your chance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Purpose of Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will leverage your knowledge of operating systems, networking, and databases to deploy, operate, support, and manage databases that support the applications delivering Takealot features. You will contribute to resolving operational issues, query improvements, and administrative tasks to provide a stable platform resilient to failures. You will also contribute to the Database team roadmap, investigating potential new technologies and designing process improvements. You demonstrate a keen interest in the latest technologies and follow database releases and security reports. You will work in a fast-paced agile environment and collaborate across both technical and non-technical teams.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;This position reports to the DBA and DataOps Engineering Manager.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot slow queries and assist developers with creating optimisable SQL queries&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist developers with schema design, schema changes, and administrative tasks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute operational excellence through metrics, monitoring, and documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and execute operational standards such as backups, replication, security, and disaster recovery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the performance, integrity, and security of corporate databases&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide ongoing maintenance and review of existing database systems to ensure optimum operation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure backups and disaster recovery systems are functional and regularly tested&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement database optimisations to improve performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage database architecture changes and ensure compliance with corporate standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with the design and administration of database cloud infrastructure as IaC&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in functional and technical specification reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute technical solutions to business problems, considering business and/or product requirements and constraints&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate with development, network, and system teams to ensure database requirements are met&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify and resolve database-related issues promptly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report on database health, performance metrics, and system improvements to stakeholders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide technical guidance to internal teams (mentoring) and external teams (collaboration)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mentor junior DBAs and engage in knowledge-sharing initiatives&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Think outside the box and explore new and/or alternative approaches to find the best solution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Minimum Required Qualification and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree in Computer Science or a related field of study, or 5–7 years of related experience&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven extensive knowledge and experience with relational databases such as MySQL or PostgreSQL, including successful deployment, management, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise with other database systems such as key-value stores, document stores, columnar databases, etc.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience with one or more non-RDBMS systems such as MongoDB, Redis, Kafka, Elasticsearch, or Solr&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven expertise in auxiliary systems such as networking, operating systems, and security&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering projects independently and/or contributing to open-source projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience collaborating on projects as part of a team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of database internals, backups, replication, metrics and monitoring, disaster recovery, security, database architecture, database configuration, query design, analysis, and optimisation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven knowledge and experience in auxiliary systems that support databases, including development and/or scripting, configuration management, networking, operating systems, data structures, cloud computing, and operations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical Skills: Proficient in database technologies (e.g., MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, Oracle). Strong understanding of database performance tuning, query optimisation, and systems architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attributes&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Problem-Solving: Effective troubleshooting and analytical skills for complex database issues&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: Strong oral and written communication skills for conveying technical content to both technical and non-technical audiences&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritisation: Ability to manage multiple database projects efficiently and meet tight deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaboration: Effective team player who can work with various teams (e.g., developers, administrators, and managers) across the organisation&lt;/li&gt;
